From: Hardik S. Panchal <quic_hpanchal@quicinc.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Jan 2022 15:21:29 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] qca-nss-eip: port IPsec client to Linux 6.18 host mode

The QSDK IPsec client combines a look-aside EIP-197 path with legacy ECM,
PPE inline-flow and packet-steering interfaces which are not available in
the Linux 6.18 qualcommbe tree. Keep the supported host look-aside path and
remove those unavailable inline dependencies.

Integrate the client with the upstream XFRM protocol multiplexers and the
EIP state-provider hooks. Preserve native ESP for unsupported states and
non-EIP packets, safely override shared NAT-T sockets, and serialize SA and
netdevice lifetimes so rekey and module teardown cannot race the data path.

Validate namespaces, marks, xfrm interfaces, offload devices, algorithms,
replay windows and migrated sequence state before claiming an SA. Add ESN,
RFC4106 salt, GSO, partial-checksum, MTU, lifetime, sequence and exact rekey
SA handling while keeping EIP hardware records and Linux XFRM accounting in
step. Use the host EIP_SVC_IPSEC service throughout the core driver.

Link: https://git.codelinaro.org/clo/qsdk/oss/lklm/nss-eip/-/tree/10a89a95f814cd325e23105f102428644f45014f
Based-on: https://git.codelinaro.org/clo/qsdk/oss/lklm/nss-eip/-/commit/d75526582ace2d06ce0d9d5b40c41a541ffb4bcb
Based-on: https://git.codelinaro.org/clo/qsdk/oss/lklm/nss-eip/-/commit/b4ee72bf8a8f36512f74afb855be7da7ca451eab
Signed-off-by: Hardik S. Panchal <quic_hpanchal@quicinc.com>
Signed-off-by: Pavithra R <quic_pavir@quicinc.com>
Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-5.6-sol
Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
